{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi","id":1512582,"title":"Homunculi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-24T08:53:07-07:00","id":1512582,"title":"Homunculi","content":"I made a take on homunculi a while ago. It might need to be adjusted for balance, and you might want to just use it for villains or make it more or less difficult, but I hope you like it:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Homunculi aren\u2019t normal monsters. They are a type of construct that can be created by anyone with the right tools. That is, assuming they know the ritual. It\u2019s fairly obscure; however, there are a number of mystic tomes that contain it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Step 1: Choose the material and craft the shape.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A homunculus can be any shape, depending on the material used to craft it. The roll to make the shape requires an extended roll of ten successes with each roll representing an hour of work. The additional benefits depend on the material.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Flesh: No effect.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Wood: +1 armor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Obsidian: 1L unarmed attacks. -1 to health.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Stone: +2 armor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Marble: +2 armor. +1 to social rolls that rely on appearance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Metal: +3 armor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Flesh homunculi require Dexterity+Medicine. All others need Dexterity+Craft.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Step 2: Attune the homunculi.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Homunculi must be magically attuned. This will determine their purpose and the stats of the homunculi, which use the character creation rules. Magically attuning the homunculi requires an extended Intelligence+Occult roll of 15 successes with each roll representing an hour of work.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Nonsentient: Nonsentient homunculi have a maximum intelligence of 1 and can only learn physical skills and intimidation; however, they blindly obey their creator\u2019s commands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Sentient: Sentient homunculi can have any intelligence and can learn any skill; however, they are their own being and, while having some loyalty to their creators, have free will.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">In both cases, you make them as a starting character after their maximum intelligence and learnable skills has been determined.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Step 3: Animating the homunculi.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This step doesn\u2019t require any rolls; however, it requires the heart of a monster. The heart will merge with the body and give the homunculi a soul. It will also give the homunculi a potency rating equal to the monster\u2019s, which gives the same willpower bonus, maximum stat and skill levels, and supernatural tolerance. Additionally, homunculi gain experience points equal to Potencyx4. They have a number of dread powers (to be decided by or in conjunction with the GM) equal to the creator\u2019s Occult dots with one additional one if they have a specialty in homunculi.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:15:22-07:00","id":1512898,"title":"","content":"Usually a homunculus is more of a clone sort of thing. I don't really know if the materials listed here are all that good. Some have drawbacks, others are just... good.<br /> <br /> I guess the question of what feedback to give would rely on what you want these to be. Are they servitors, or are they something more like Prometheans without the baggage? Because even someone with <i>literal</i> marble skin is going to have trouble interacting with humans, so that Striking Looks won't be much use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:01:33-07:00","id":1512951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1512898#post1512898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually a homunculus is more of a clone sort of thing. I don't really know if the materials listed here are all that good. Some have drawbacks, others are just... good.<br /> <br /> I guess the question of what feedback to give would rely on what you want these to be. Are they servitors, or are they something more like Prometheans without the baggage? Because even someone with <i>literal</i> marble skin is going to have trouble interacting with humans, so that Striking Looks won't be much use.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're more meant to be servitors with the more intelligent ones having sentience, maybe being slightly more like prometheans but not really. They also aren't intended to be player characters. Instead, they're meant to be NPCs who serve people like sorcerers and maybe player characters. They're also meant to be somewhat difficult to create as well, given that you need to kill monsters to make them. And some materials are meant to be better than others. The idea is that better materials make better homunculi.<br /> <br /> As for the name, these things honestly resemble golems more than homunculi and are meant to. But I decided to not call them golems because golems are a thing in MTA while homunuli, as far as I could find in the book and other COFD books, aren't. But I could have missed them. So, think of them with their name changed to golems to get the most accurate picture.<br /> <br /> And you have a good point that marble skin would have difficulty interacting with normal people. Maybe that bonus would only apply to those aware of and accepting of the supernatural and would become a penalty around people not aware of and accepting of the supernatural? The marble could be something that spellcasters use to show off to other spellcasters and similar things more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:40:50-07:00","id":1512956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1512951#post1512951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the name, these things honestly resemble golems more than homunculi and are meant to. But I decided to not call them golems because golems are a thing in MTA while homunuli, as far as I could find in the book and other COFD books, aren't. But I could have missed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage 1e supplement Tome of the Mysteries contains detailed spells for the construction of homunculi on pages 149-152 as part of its section on alchemy. The section on adding an Armor rating to a homunculus notes that highly armored specimens are sometimes referred to as golems.<br /> <br /> The two main spells for homunculus construction don't work as-written in 2e's spellcasting model, being extended actions whose large number of potential required successes can be accumulated at over multiple efforts, but this <i>does</i> mean they scan fairly well to 2e's model of ordinary extended actions, particularly when filtered through the extended version of the Craft Equipment action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:41:55-07:00","id":1512980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1512956#post1512956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage 1e supplement Tome of the Mysteries contains detailed spells for the construction of homunculi on pages 149-152 as part of its section on alchemy. The section on adding an Armor rating to a homunculus notes that highly armored specimens are sometimes referred to as golems.<br /> <br /> The two main spells for homunculus construction don't work as-written in 2e's spellcasting model, being extended actions whose large number of potential required successes can be accumulated at over multiple efforts, but this <i>does</i> mean they scan fairly well to 2e's model of ordinary extended actions, particularly when filtered through the extended version of the Craft Equipment action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never had Mage 1e or its supplements, so I didn't know it had homunculi. And, while it has homunculi, my homunculi rules are meant to be more of a ritual that anyone can use. The sort of thing that a seemingly unassuming person with no magical powers but knowledge of a few rituals could make, for various reasons connected to types of horror, such as building paranoia. I just didn't want to call them golems because Mage had that word taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T18:23:02-07:00","id":1513022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1512980#post1512980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, while it has homunculi, my homunculi rules are meant to be more of a ritual that anyone can use. The sort of thing that a seemingly unassuming person with no magical powers but knowledge of a few rituals could make, for various reasons connected to types of horror, such as building paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why I said that the mechanics for the unusual spells presented in Tome of the Mysteries to accomplish this \u2014 which no longer work as-written thanks to Mage: the Awakening 2e having all spells resolved as an instant action \u2014 could make for a useful basis for the Revised Storytelling System's approach to Extended Actions, particularly as it relates to crafting.<br /> <br /> The three principal spells for making a homunculus that isn't animated by an ephemeral being are an extended action to create the form \u2014 this roll requires an alchemical lab to perform, and its successes go toward a number of factors, including its Size, whether it counts a person for the purposes of spells that target people (and if so, how long its lifespan is), Physical Attributes and Skills, Armor, and natural weaponry, with each failed roll introducing a noticeable imperfection into the homunculus's form and the degree to which the homunculus resembles the human mages who participated in its creation affects the degeneration roll each of those mages has to make \u2014 an extended action to create the personality of the homunculus \u2014 including its Mental and Social Attributes and Skills, the degree of loyalty it has towards its owner, the number of additional people it takes orders from, and which derangements and Flaws (if any) it can be known to manifest if the animation process doesn't go perfectly \u2014 and an instant action to animate the proto-homunculus with its designed form and personality.<br /> <br /> Given all of the above, it may be prudent to not have the process boil down to a pair of fixed-target extended action rolls with an interval of an hour regardless of what the homunculus's stats are, especially since you're referencing using Horror systems like Potency and Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just didn't want to call them golems because Mage had that word taken. </div> </div> </div>Promethean has also had that word taken, so the ship has kind of sailed in that regard.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, considering about half of the monsters that have published gamelines about them and many others besides don't have souls in game-mechanical terms, it may be prudent to define what is meant by &quot;gives the homunculus a soul.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T06:44:39-07:00","id":1513068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513022#post1513022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, which is why I said that the mechanics for the unusual spells presented in Tome of the Mysteries to accomplish this \u2014 which no longer work as-written thanks to Mage: the Awakening 2e having all spells resolved as an instant action \u2014 could make for a useful basis for the Revised Storytelling System's approach to Extended Actions, particularly as it relates to crafting.<br /> <br /> The three principal spells for making a homunculus that isn't animated by an ephemeral being are an extended action to create the form \u2014 this roll requires an alchemical lab to perform, and its successes go toward a number of factors, including its Size, whether it counts a person for the purposes of spells that target people (and if so, how long its lifespan is), Physical Attributes and Skills, Armor, and natural weaponry, with each failed roll introducing a noticeable imperfection into the homunculus's form and the degree to which the homunculus resembles the human mages who participated in its creation affects the degeneration roll each of those mages has to make \u2014 an extended action to create the personality of the homunculus \u2014 including its Mental and Social Attributes and Skills, the degree of loyalty it has towards its owner, the number of additional people it takes orders from, and which derangements and Flaws (if any) it can be known to manifest if the animation process doesn't go perfectly \u2014 and an instant action to animate the proto-homunculus with its designed form and personality.<br /> <br /> Given all of the above, it may be prudent to not have the process boil down to a pair of fixed-target extended action rolls with an interval of an hour regardless of what the homunculus's stats are, especially since you're referencing using Horror systems like Potency and Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> Promethean has also had that word taken, so the ship has kind of sailed in that regard.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, considering about half of the monsters that have published gamelines about them and many others besides don't have souls in game-mechanical terms, it may be prudent to define what is meant by &quot;gives the homunculus a soul.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You make some very good points.<br /> <br /> So, how about this:<br /> For the soul part, maybe we could change it so that it just says that the heart brings the homunculus to life? It'd be less confusing and leave more up to the GM regarding whether or not homunculi have souls.<br /> <br /> As for the fixed-target rolls, that's another good point. So, how about these for starting changes:<br /> Rather than a fixed number of successes, the target number of successes for the Crafts roll could depent on the materials used?<br /> Like:<br /> Flesh: 1 success.<br /> Wood or obsidian: 2 successes.<br /> Stone or marble: 3 successes.<br /> Metal: 4 successes.<br /> That way, the better materials have a cost to them.<br /> <br /> As for the Occult roll, perhaps the target successes could be equal to the Potency of the homunculus? That way, more powerful homunculi are more difficult to make all around?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of special materials being required as well. At the very least, they should need a workspace with fitting equipment for crafting the homunculus' body and making it so that the heart will animate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T09:02:19-07:00","id":1513079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513068#post1513068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the soul part, maybe we could change it so that it just says that the heart brings the homunculus to life? It'd be less confusing and leave more up to the GM regarding whether or not homunculi have souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bit is reasonable. The next questions then are &quot;What counts as a monster for this purpose?&quot; and &quot;What counts as a heart for this purpose?&quot; i.e. Can a piece of a spirit-Claimed or a mortal psychic empower a homunculus? What about a monster with no humanoid form or origin? Does the &quot;heart&quot; have to be the organ in the chest of a living being or can the motherboard of an evil computer serve the same purpose? Can a manifested ghost (or one bound into one of its Anchors) do the trick?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the fixed-target rolls, that's another good point. So, how about these for starting changes:<br /> Rather than a fixed number of successes, the target number of successes for the Crafts roll could depent on the materials used?<br /> Like:<br /> Flesh: 1 success.<br /> Wood or obsidian: 2 successes.<br /> Stone or marble: 3 successes.<br /> Metal: 4 successes.<br /> That way, the better materials have a cost to them. </div> </div> </div>I note that this hierarchy maps pretty straightforwardly to Durability (which itself translates to weapon bonus and/or Armor rating for characters), so it may be sensible to set the base cost as Size x [Durability + 1] with potential extra modifiers like Availability, depending on how you want the biases of creation to skew, i.e. is a homunculus made of gold more or less desirable than a homunculus made with equally durable metal, or does that not matter?<br /> <br /> By a similar token, it's probably worth addressing whether Dread Powers modeling physical capabilities ought to be part of the body-construction roll instead of the attunement roll or the animation process \u2014 and whether the creation's &quot;natural&quot; weapons and armor already count toward the limit of Dread Powers, particularly if homunculus creation is something theoretically anyone with the right knowledge can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Occult roll, perhaps the target successes could be equal to the Potency of the homunculus? That way, more powerful homunculi are more difficult to make all around?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of special materials being required as well. At the very least, they should need a workspace with fitting equipment for crafting the homunculus' body and making it so that the heart will animate it. </div> </div> </div>Obviously in the model where the Potency of the contributing monster directly translates to the Potency of the homunculus this is less of a concern, but it's probably also worth treating the donor's Potency as an upper limit that the homunculus's creator can fall short of or aim below to have better odds of completing the project before they run out of extended rolls. Maybe make donor Potency in excess of target Potency count as bonus successes towards the attunement roll or other step of the process? (If more expensive parts are more desirable, maybe have Availability factor in in a similar fashion?)<br /> <br /> There's not a direct mundanely-accessible equivalent of Alchemical Lab in 2e, but Safe Place, Resources, and appropriate Library dots can probably contribute to the roll and/or target number adjustment in some way as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T15:55:15-07:00","id":1513128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513079#post1513079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That bit is reasonable. The next questions then are &quot;What counts as a monster for this purpose?&quot; and &quot;What counts as a heart for this purpose?&quot; i.e. Can a piece of a spirit-Claimed or a mortal psychic empower a homunculus? What about a monster with no humanoid form or origin? Does the &quot;heart&quot; have to be the organ in the chest of a living being or can the motherboard of an evil computer serve the same purpose? Can a manifested ghost (or one bound into one of its Anchors) do the trick?<br /> <br /> I note that this hierarchy maps pretty straightforwardly to Durability (which itself translates to weapon bonus and/or Armor rating for characters), so it may be sensible to set the base cost as Size x [Durability + 1] with potential extra modifiers like Availability, depending on how you want the biases of creation to skew, i.e. is a homunculus made of gold more or less desirable than a homunculus made with equally durable metal, or does that not matter?<br /> <br /> By a similar token, it's probably worth addressing whether Dread Powers modeling physical capabilities ought to be part of the body-construction roll instead of the attunement roll or the animation process \u2014 and whether the creation's &quot;natural&quot; weapons and armor already count toward the limit of Dread Powers, particularly if homunculus creation is something theoretically anyone with the right knowledge can do.<br /> <br /> Obviously in the model where the Potency of the contributing monster directly translates to the Potency of the homunculus this is less of a concern, but it's probably also worth treating the donor's Potency as an upper limit that the homunculus's creator can fall short of or aim below to have better odds of completing the project before they run out of extended rolls. Maybe make donor Potency in excess of target Potency count as bonus successes towards the attunement roll or other step of the process? (If more expensive parts are more desirable, maybe have Availability factor in in a similar fashion?)<br /> <br /> There's not a direct mundanely-accessible equivalent of Alchemical Lab in 2e, but Safe Place, Resources, and appropriate Library dots can probably contribute to the roll and/or target number adjustment in some way as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>What counts as a monster is anything with a supernatural power rating. So, something with Potency, Primal Urge, Primum, etc. And the heart has to be the physical organ. So, only things with literal hearts count.<br /> <br /> Homunculi don't have durability like machines. Still, you make a good point about size. Maybe making it smaller or larger size needs less or more successes? They are, for gameplay purposes, living characters. And as for whether or not gold should be different than any other metal, logically it should. However, in terms of gameplay mechanics, I think it might make things a bit too complicated.<br /> <br /> But you're making another good point about Dread Powers. The armor that homunculi get from their metals wouldn't count, but someone could mold in weapons and other things. Going by your previous idea, maybe various mechanical things could be put into homunculi, such as claws or a sword arm? These would require extra successes to make, and they wouldn't count as dread powers.<br /> <br /> I like the upper limit idea too. So, yeah, let's make it so that you can reduce the homunculi's potency to get bonus successes. Or at least bonus dice.<br /> <br /> And I think those could work. Safe Place could reduce the number of target dots while resources and library can increase the number of dice you roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T16:27:32-07:00","id":1513132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513128#post1513128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homunculi don't have durability like machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the material they're made out of can and that can scan directly to Armor ratings and weapon damage, which is why I was suggesting that the Durability rating of the material (0 for flesh, hence the +1 in the posited formula, which could instead be &quot;minimum 1&quot; if you don't want flesh-based homunculi to be faster to construct than wooden ones) could serve as the main scalar of difficulty in constructing a homunculus's form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, you make a good point about size. Maybe making it smaller or larger size needs less or more successes? They are, for gameplay purposes, living characters. And as for whether or not gold should be different than any other metal, logically it should. However, in terms of gameplay mechanics, I think it might make things a bit too complicated. </div> </div> </div>Size feels important, not least because the term &quot;homunculus&quot; literally refers to a little person and it's notionally simpler to fit artificial &quot;life&quot; into the setting if the more-common-by-ease specimens are small enough to hide.<br /> <br /> I ask about gold as an example because it affects the bias of how homunculi made with this process are constructed \u2014 if rare materials and precisely-designed parts (i.e stuff that would be expensive or otherwise difficult to source) are often necessary for a person to manage to successfully make a homunculus, their creators can be assumed to be rich or otherwise have some means of getting access to those components, whereas if they provide desirable qualities to the outcome (e.g. if you need appropriate materials for the homunculus to manifest certain Dread Powers) then simple constructs can be produced without necessitating wealth and/or criminal behavior<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think those could work. Safe Place could reduce the number of target dots while resources and library can increase the number of dice you roll? </div> </div> </div>Library directly adds bonus dice to extended rolls with a Mental Skill as-written, but I think Safe Place would probably work better by increasing the number of rolls allowed. Resources reducing the target number feels sensible, but so does making use of the Merit's rules for purchases such that e.g. each roll or each failure counts as a purchase of Availability equal to the target Potency (or requires an equivalently intensive use of Skills or Social Merits, if not using Resources).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T08:42:16-07:00","id":1513198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513132#post1513132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but the material they're made out of can and that can scan directly to Armor ratings and weapon damage, which is why I was suggesting that the Durability rating of the material (0 for flesh, hence the +1 in the posited formula, which could instead be &quot;minimum 1&quot; if you don't want flesh-based homunculi to be faster to construct than wooden ones) could serve as the main scalar of difficulty in constructing a homunculus's form.<br /> <br /> Size feels important, not least because the term &quot;homunculus&quot; literally refers to a little person and it's notionally simpler to fit artificial &quot;life&quot; into the setting if the more-common-by-ease specimens are small enough to hide.<br /> <br /> I ask about gold as an example because it affects the bias of how homunculi made with this process are constructed \u2014 if rare materials and precisely-designed parts (i.e stuff that would be expensive or otherwise difficult to source) are often necessary for a person to manage to successfully make a homunculus, their creators can be assumed to be rich or otherwise have some means of getting access to those components, whereas if they provide desirable qualities to the outcome (e.g. if you need appropriate materials for the homunculus to manifest certain Dread Powers) then simple constructs can be produced without necessitating wealth and/or criminal behavior<br /> <br /> Library directly adds bonus dice to extended rolls with a Mental Skill as-written, but I think Safe Place would probably work better by increasing the number of rolls allowed. Resources reducing the target number feels sensible, but so does making use of the Merit's rules for purchases such that e.g. each roll or each failure counts as a purchase of Availability equal to the target Potency (or requires an equivalently intensive use of Skills or Social Merits, if not using Resources).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point. Durability is an easy rating. So, yeah, let's go with durability increasing the difficulty.<br /> <br /> That's another good point about size. So, having a smaller size require less successes would encourage that.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about gold and rare materials being necessary would add much to this. It could, but you need to kill monsters to create these homunculi in the first place. And if you want a powerful homunculus, you need to kill a powerful monster. That already says a lot about the people capable of making these homunculi. That and I don't want to make the system too complicated. This is meant to be relatively simple.<br /> <br /> Those are good points too. Let's go with Safe Place increasing the number of rolls allowed. As for Resources, that's a good idea too. I'd personally prefer it if it was kept to reducing the target number to keep things simple, but we could have that bit in as well as an optional system so GMs can decide which they prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:13:31-07:00","id":1513406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1512951#post1512951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the name, these things honestly resemble golems more than homunculi and are meant to. But I decided to not call them golems because golems are a thing in MTA while homunuli, as far as I could find in the book and other COFD books, aren't..</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the word &quot;Demon&quot; is used about a hundred times to mean a hundred different things. Beasts are both a Changeling type and a splat. I wouldn't really worry about that.<br /> <br /> I actually had a power I made <i>aaaages</i> ago that might fit, since it explicitly creates a homunculus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Body Impolitic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aspect of Vicissitude that tends to disgust those without the Tzimisce\u2019s sense of beauty, this ability allows the voivode to create a homunculus and bestow it with a semblance of life. Over the course of an hour per dot of Size, the Tzimisce grows a fleshy tumour by spending two vitae that detaches itself and forms a servitor. The servitor, which has a Size no more than the voivode\u2019s Blood Potency, functions as the Retainer merit equal to the creator\u2019s Protean dots. The function of the homunculus (which determines it\u2019s dice pools) is determined when it\u2019s made, though no matter how adept the creator is at Protean, the fleshworked creature will always have the mind of a child, even if it rolls ten dice to perform its task.<br /> While some voivode will create stunning diminutive faeries, others will craft hideous grotesqueries that only their creator can love. A Tzimisce that grows attached to her adorable little abomination may ghoul it, granting it the ability to learn Disciplines of its own, including Vicissitude. The living teratoma can hold vitae equal to its dot rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIgnore that it was from an attempt to bring Vicissitude into 2e. But I also assume that &quot;use the Retainer mechanics&quot; probably isn't what you're wanting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T06:36:16-07:00","id":1513529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512582-homunculi?p=1513406#post1513406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the word &quot;Demon&quot; is used about a hundred times to mean a hundred different things. Beasts are both a Changeling type and a splat. I wouldn't really worry about that.<br /> <br /> I actually had a power I made <i>aaaages</i> ago that might fit, since it explicitly creates a homunculus:<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bIgnore that it was from an attempt to bring Vicissitude into 2e. But I also assume that &quot;use the Retainer mechanics&quot; probably isn't what you're wanting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it isn't quite what I'm looking for. The homunculi are meant to be more powerful servitors than what the retainer mechanic can get. Each one of them is created from killing a monster, after all, so they should be fairly special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}